# An allowlist. Everything stays out of the build context except what the Dockerfile copies, so .env (real AWS
# credentials), the 5 GB .venv, and the photos/ and jobdir/ that scripts/dev/worker-reconstruct.sh leaves here can't
# reach an image, even through a future broad COPY. A file the Dockerfile needs but this list leaves out fails its COPY
# line outright, so a gap can't pass silently.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!pipeline/
!run_job.py

# Re-excluded inside pipeline/, which the allowlist above lets back in whole. Patterns match from the context root, not
# at every level the way .gitignore's do, so each needs the **/ prefix.
**/__pycache__/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
